| **Hold** | How long the clip stays after each run of words. | 1.5 s | 0 to 5 s | 0.5, 1, 1.5, 3 |
| **Fade** | How long the clip takes to fade out and in. At 0 it's a straight cut. | 0.3 s | 0 to 5 s | 0, 0.15, 0.3, 0.5 |

The fades sit outside the other two. The clip starts to fade out when **Hold** ends, and it finishes fading in **Pre-roll** before the first word.

So short pauses never hide the clip. A pause no longer than **Pre-roll** plus **Hold** leaves it on screen, which is 1.7 s at the defaults. The clip only fades all the way out in a pause of at least **Pre-roll** plus **Hold** plus two **Fades**, which is 2.3 s. Anything in between is a partial dip.

Each change is one undo step, called Hide While Silent. These rows belong to the clip, even with an [action](/motion/actions/) selected.

## See it on the timeline

A teal line runs across the picture part of the clip. Where it's at the top, the clip shows. Where it's at the bottom, the clip is hidden. The clip has to be [tall enough](/timeline/track-height/) to show the line.

Inside an open [nest](/editing/nests/), a clip that follows a file outside the nest doesn't draw its line, though it still fades. See [Reading a clip on the timeline](/timeline/reading-a-clip/).

